# ---- 822 Welding III ----
H("822.d.1.A",3,"Keisha plans to apply to a Texas welding technology program. She compares entrance requirements, tuition and the exams she must pass first. She is determining:","academic knowledge and skills required for postsecondary education",["only the weather at the campus","only the football team","only the dorm colors"],"Entry requirements guide planning.")
H("822.d.1.A",4,"Which activity best helps a junior prepare for a college-level welding program?","completing algebra and geometry while building weld test coupons",["dropping all math classes","avoiding the shop","skipping career fairs"],"Math and hands-on practice both count.")
H("822.d.1.B",3,"The owner of a machine repair shop says repeat customers come from quick turnaround and welds that do not crack. These employer expectations promote:","positive customer satisfaction",["higher turnover","more complaints","fewer orders"],"Satisfied customers return.")
H("822.d.1.B",4,"A customer asks a welder to match the color and finish of an old gate. The best way to meet the expectation is to:","confirm the details and show a sample before finishing",["guess the color","skip the finish","tell the customer to do it"],"Confirm requirements.")
H("822.d.1.C",3,"During a mock job interview, Andre shakes hands, answers with eye contact and brings copies of his certifications. This demonstrates professional standards such as:","interviewing skills",["tardiness","distraction","avoidance"],"Interviews are a professional standard.")
H("822.d.1.C",4,"Which item should a welder bring to an employment interview?","a résumé and copies of certifications",["a bag of scrap","a grinder","nothing at all"],"Documents show qualifications.")
H("822.d.1.D",3,"Every six weeks, Marcus compares his certifications and test results to the list he wrote for his career goal. He is evaluating:","progress toward personal career goals",["his lunch plans","next year's prices","a coworker's pay"],"Compare progress with goals.")
H("822.d.1.D",4,"Marcus notices he is behind on his hours toward an inspector credential. His best next step is to:","adjust his schedule to add hours",["drop the goal","hide the record","wait without a plan"],"Use the evaluation to adjust.")
H("822.d.1.E",3,"Before the night crew starts a pipe job, the lead walks through the drawing, the joint prep and the inspection point with each welder. This is communicating to:","clarify objectives in the workplace",["slow the schedule","complicate the job","avoid training"],"Briefings align the team.")
H("822.d.1.E",4,"A welder is unsure which pass sequence the supervisor wants. The best communication choice is to:","ask for the written procedure and confirm it",["pick a sequence at random","wait silently","skip the job"],"Clarify the procedure.")
H("822.d.1.F",3,"A shop keeps a first-aid kit, posts emergency exits and trains workers in lockout/tagout. These practices apply:","health and safety knowledge as specified by OSHA",["marketing rules","sales quotas","parking rules"],"OSHA safety knowledge.")
H("822.d.1.F",4,"If a welder gets a flash burn in the eyes, the best action is to:","seek first aid and report the incident",["keep working","rub the eyes","ignore it until tomorrow"],"Report and treat injuries.")
H("822.d.2.A",3,"A shop owner needs the cost of 12 brackets that use 3 ft of angle at $4 per ft each, plus $18 in wire for the whole job. The estimate is:","$162",["$144","$48","$216"],"12×3×4 = 144; +18 = 162.")
H("822.d.2.A",4,"A job needs 40 hours of labor at $32 an hour, $560 of material and 15% overhead on the total. The estimate is:","$2,116",["$1,840","$1,900","$2,208"],"1,280+560=1,840; ×1.15 = 2,116.")
H("822.d.2.B",3,"If a welder misreads a tape and cuts every beam 1/4 in. too long, the cost estimate will be:","too low because of waste and rework not planned",["exact","too high because of savings","unaffected"],"Errors add waste and rework.")
H("822.d.2.B",4,"Accurate readings of measuring devices reduce costs mainly by:","reducing scrap and rework",["increasing scrap","adding delay","hiding errors"],"Accuracy saves money.")
H("822.d.2.C",3,"To check the thickness of a plate to the nearest thousandth of an inch, a welder should choose a:","micrometer",["yardstick","tape measure","carpenter's rule"],"Micrometers read thousandths.")
H("822.d.2.C",4,"Justify the choice of a long tape measure rather than a caliper to check a 20-ft beam: the tape is better because it:","can measure long lengths reasonably accurately",["measures thousandths","fits in a pocket only","never needs reading"],"Match tool to task.")
H("822.d.2.D",3,"A cylinder 10 in. across (radius 5 in.) is 8 in. tall. Using π ≈ 3.14, its volume is closest to:","628 cubic inches",["314 cubic inches","251 cubic inches","400 cubic inches"],"3.14×25×8 = 628.")
H("822.d.2.D",4,"The perimeter of a rectangular frame 30 in. by 18 in. is:","96 in.",["48 in.","540 in.","66 in."],"2×(30+18) = 96.")
H("822.d.2.E",3,"A welder adds 6 3/8 in., 4.5 in. and 2 1/8 in. The total is:","13 in.",["12 in.","13 3/8 in.","14 in."],"6.375+4.5+2.125 = 13.")
H("822.d.2.E",4,"A welder must cut 7/8 in. from each of 6 identical pieces. The total length removed is:","5 1/4 in.",["4 3/4 in.","5 in.","5 1/2 in."],"6×0.875 = 5.25.")
H("822.d.2.F",3,"A ramp frame has a base of 12 ft and a rise of 5 ft. The sloped length is:","13 ft",["17 ft","7 ft","15 ft"],"144+25=169; √169=13.")
H("822.d.2.F",4,"A diagonal brace runs 9 ft on one leg and 12 ft on the other. Its length is:","15 ft",["21 ft","18 ft","13 ft"],"81+144=225; √225=15.")
H("822.d.2.G",3,"To estimate the amount of steel needed for a rectangular plate, the best formula is:","length times width times thickness",["length plus width","width divided by length","length minus thickness"],"Volume of a rectangular solid.")
H("822.d.2.G",4,"To estimate weld metal for a groove joint, the cross-sectional area of the groove is multiplied by the:","length of the joint",["color of the plate","brand of the wire","shift time"],"Volume = area × length.")
H("822.d.3.A",3,"Before running a job, Tasha checks that guards are in place and the machine's cable and ground are in good condition. She is:","using welding equipment according to safety standards",["selling equipment","ignoring standards","moving the shop"],"Pre-use checks.")
H("822.d.3.A",4,"A welder finds a cracked cable lug on the machine. The correct step is to:","tag it out of service until repaired",["tape it","use it anyway","hide it"],"Defective equipment is removed.")
H("822.d.3.B",3,"A spent can of cleaning solvent and contaminated rags from the shop should be:","placed in approved waste containers for hazardous disposal",["dumped outside","put in the regular trash","poured into the drain"],"Dispose hazardous waste properly.")
H("822.d.3.B",4,"Disposing of used solvent in a storm drain is wrong because it can:","contaminate soil and water supplies",["improve soil","help plants grow","purify water"],"Hazardous materials pollute.")
H("822.d.3.C",3,"A fabrication shop recycles scrap steel, copper and aluminum off-cuts instead of landfilling them. A student explains this saves:","raw materials, energy and landfill space",["only time","nothing","only paint"],"Recycling conserves resources.")
H("822.d.3.C",4,"Which statement correctly describes recycling in a welding shop?","separating metals by type makes recycling more efficient",["mixing all metals is best","burying scrap is best","avoid separating"],"Sorted scrap is worth more.")
H("822.d.3.D",3,"A company tests a new welding power source with pulsed waveforms and compares weld quality and speed with its old machine. This is evaluating:","the performance impact of an emerging technology",["an old tradition","a payroll plan","a uniform"],"New tech is judged on performance.")
H("822.d.3.D",4,"A real benefit that can result from new welding technology is:","faster production with consistent weld quality",["slower output","poorer control","more scrap"],"Emerging technologies improve efficiency.")
H("822.d.3.E",3,"Following the shop's safety measures, a welder puts on a flame-resistant jacket, safety glasses under the helmet and hearing protection near the grinders. She is:","using appropriate personal protective equipment",["ignoring safety","ordering parts","arranging a meeting"],"PPE follows safety measures.")
H("822.d.3.E",4,"Welding in a closed space with poor airflow, the worker should add:","a respirator or forced ventilation",["a heavier jacket only","more heat","more rods"],"Fume protection.")
H("822.d.3.F",3,"A shop investigates robots that weld the same bracket thousands of times, programmed by numerical control and computer files. This is learning about:","automated welding machines",["manual painting","hand drawing","office filing"],"Automation uses numerical control.")
H("822.d.3.F",4,"A common reason a shop adds an automated welding cell is to:","achieve consistent welds on repeated parts",["avoid all inspection","stop using electricity","eliminate quality checks"],"Automation gives repeatability.")
H("822.d.4.A",3,"A student reads the print, the bill of materials and the tolerances to build a trailer hitch project from start to finish. She is using:","knowledge of engineering drawings to complete an advanced project",["guessing","memory only","a coin toss"],"Drawings guide the build.")
H("822.d.4.A",4,"A bill of materials on a drawing lists:","the parts and quantities needed",["the customer's lunch","the welder's pay","the shop's address only"],"BOMs list parts.")
H("822.d.4.B",3,"After finishing a bracket, Noor checks each dimension and weld size against the drawing. She is:","evaluating the project using drawing specifications",["painting the part","packing the part","pricing the part"],"Compare finished work to the print.")
H("822.d.4.B",4,"If a measured hole is outside the tolerance on the print, the part should be:","reworked or rejected according to the specification",["shipped as is","hidden","painted over"],"Out-of-tolerance parts fail.")
H("822.d.5.A",3,"Given a print and material, Luis fabricates a small steel table with little help from the instructor. He is:","working independently to fabricate a welded project",["only copying a coworker","avoiding the print","waiting for help"],"Independent fabrication.")
H("822.d.5.A",4,"When fabricating independently, a welder should still:","verify the fit-up and dimensions before welding",["skip layout","ignore the print","guess dimensions"],"Check before welding.")
H("822.d.5.B",3,"Two students split a job to build a trailer, one cutting and fitting, the other welding and inspecting, and then swap roles. They are:","working collaboratively on a real-world project",["working against each other","working alone","avoiding the job"],"Collaboration on real projects.")
H("822.d.5.B",4,"A good practice when two welders share one project is to:","agree on the sequence and communicate before moving parts",["move parts without notice","work without talking","ignore the other welder"],"Communication prevents accidents.")
H("822.d.5.C",3,"A wire welder starts to feed erratically and the arc sputters. Valeria checks the drive rolls, liner and tension. She is:","troubleshooting equipment",["selling equipment","ignoring the problem","drawing a part"],"Systematic troubleshooting.")
H("822.d.5.C",4,"A stick welder will not strike an arc. The first thing to check is:","the ground clamp connection and cable",["the shop's lights","the customer's invoice","the paint color"],"Poor ground is a common cause.")
H("822.d.7.A",3,"Before cutting with oxy-fuel, Imani clears flammables, wears eye protection and keeps an extinguisher close. She is:","observing safe operating practices",["skipping steps","speeding up","ignoring risks"],"Cutting safety.")
H("822.d.7.A",4,"Sparks from cutting can travel many feet, so the operator should:","remove or cover combustibles within the work zone",["ignore the sparks","leave rags nearby","remove the extinguisher"],"Hot work precautions.")
H("822.d.7.B",3,"After the shift, a cylinder cart is secured upright, valves closed and caps on. This shows:","safe handling of compressed gases",["unsafe handling","wasteful handling","random handling"],"Cylinder safety.")
H("822.d.7.B",4,"Oxygen cylinders and fuel gas cylinders in storage should be:","separated and secured upright",["stored together without separation","left lying down","stored near heat"],"Separate and secure.")
H("822.d.7.C",3,"A student follows an accepted standard to pierce, cut a straight line and bevel an edge in plate. She is performing cutting processes:","according to accepted welding standards",["in random order","by guess","without safety"],"Standards define good cuts.")
H("822.d.7.C",4,"A bevel cut prepares plate for:","a groove weld",["painting","drilling only","storage"],"Bevels enable groove welds.")
H("822.d.8.A",3,"Before an overhead weld, Gabe checks his gloves, jacket and cap and puts a cap over his helmet to keep sparks out of his hair. He is:","employing safe operating practices",["ignoring risks","speeding up","skipping steps"],"Overhead welding safety.")
H("822.d.8.A",4,"Overhead welding creates a hazard of:","falling sparks and molten metal",["cooler air","extra gas","less light"],"Dress to shed sparks.")
H("822.d.8.B",3,"To pass a qualification test, Hana welds coupons in flat, horizontal, vertical and overhead positions and meets the standard's criteria. She is:","making welds in all positions according to industry standards",["only tacking","avoiding standards","doing it once"],"Qualification tests require all positions.")
H("822.d.8.B",4,"A welder qualification test is judged by:","visual inspection and bend or other tests per the code",["a coin toss","the welder's guess","the appearance of the helmet"],"Tests follow the code.")
H("822.d.9.A",3,"Before a wire-feed job, Omar secures the cylinder, checks the gas flow and clears the area of flammables. He is:","using safe operating practices",["ignoring safety","skipping steps","guessing"],"GMAW safety.")
H("822.d.9.A",4,"Leaking shielding gas in a small closed room is dangerous because it can:","displace oxygen",["add oxygen","cool the metal","improve weld quality"],"Inert gases displace oxygen.")
H("822.d.9.B",3,"A student welds a T-joint and a beveled V-groove joint with wire feed. She is performing:","fillet and groove welds",["only cutting","only grinding","only painting"],"Basic joint types.")
H("822.d.9.B",4,"Which joint requires beveling the plate edges before welding?","a V-groove butt joint on thick plate",["a thin lap joint","a surface weld","a spot weld on sheet"],"Thick butt joints need prep.")
H("822.d.9.C",3,"On a certification test, a welder must weld in each assigned position and pass the bend test. This demonstrates welding in:","all appropriate positions according to industry-accepted standards",["one position only","any position without limits","no position"],"Certification covers positions.")
H("822.d.9.C",4,"Which statement about welding positions on a certification test is correct?","the position is stated by the test code and must be followed",["welders may choose any","positions do not matter","the helmet decides"],"The code determines the positions.")
H("822.d.10.A",3,"Before running a TIG job on stainless, Rae clears the solvents, checks the gas and wears the correct lens. She is:","employing safe operating practices",["ignoring safety","skipping steps","speeding up"],"GTAW safety.")
H("822.d.10.A",4,"The arc light from TIG welding is intense, so the welder should:","wear a helmet with the proper shade lens",["look away only","use sunglasses","wear nothing"],"Eye protection.")
H("822.d.10.B",3,"A welder runs fillet and groove welds in the flat, vertical and overhead positions using TIG. She is:","performing fillet and groove welds in all positions",["only flat welding","only brazing","only cutting"],"All-position practice.")
H("822.d.10.B",4,"TIG welding is often chosen for thin metals because it:","allows precise heat control",["cannot control heat","burns through quickly","needs no skill"],"Precise control.")
H("822.d.10.C",3,"A shop welds a stainless tank, an aluminum frame and a carbon steel pipe in the same week, selecting the filler and settings for each. This is performing welds on:","a variety of metals",["only one metal","wood","glass"],"Different metals need different settings.")
H("822.d.10.C",4,"Aluminum is commonly TIG welded with:","alternating current and argon shielding",["direct current only with no gas","acetylene","oxygen only"],"AC cleans the oxide.")

# ---- 823 Welding IV ----
H("823.d.1.A",3,"A welder writes a short email to a supervisor explaining that a plate arrived 1/8 in. undersized and asks how to proceed. The email works well because it is:","clear, concise and effective",["long and vague","angry and rushed","full of slang"],"Good writing is clear and brief.")
H("823.d.1.A",4,"Which sentence best expresses an idea in a clear, concise manner?","The 3/8 in. plate failed the bend test; please advise on a retest.",["Stuff went wrong with the plate and things.","Something happened, you know.","It's all messed up, whatever."],"Specific and brief.")
H("823.d.1.B",3,"A lead writes work instructions with numbered steps, units and a sketch so that any new hire can follow them. This is conveying written information that is:","easily understandable to others",["confusing","incomplete","hidden"],"Steps and sketches clarify.")
H("823.d.1.B",4,"A welder's written note about a repair should include:","what was done, where and when",["only a complaint","only the weather","no details"],"Useful records are specific.")
H("823.d.1.C",3,"Sam reports to work on time, stays through the end of the shift, and finishes every task assigned. He is demonstrating:","acceptable work ethics",["poor habits","avoidance","laziness"],"Reliability is a work ethic.")
H("823.d.1.C",4,"A welder who will be late because of a car problem should:","call the supervisor as early as possible",["say nothing","blame a coworker","skip work without notice"],"Communicate absences.")
H("823.d.1.D",3,"On a job site, Dee wears clean PPE, uses respectful language with the inspector and keeps her cell phone put away while working. She is conducting herself:","in a manner acceptable for the profession and work site",["casually","rudely","unsafely"],"Professional conduct.")
H("823.d.1.D",4,"Which behavior is appropriate on a welding job site?","following dress code and speaking respectfully",["arguing with customers","ignoring the dress code","using phones during welding"],"Professionalism at work.")
H("823.d.1.E",3,"A welder finds that a coworker has signed off a weld without inspection. Choosing the ethical action, she should:","report it to the supervisor following company policy",["hide it","sign it too","ignore the rules"],"Integrity and compliance.")
H("823.d.1.E",4,"Falsifying a weld inspection record is:","unethical and may be illegal",["acceptable","a shortcut","required by codes"],"Honesty is required.")
H("823.d.1.F",3,"A quality technician reviews every field on a weld procedure, from the preheat temperature to the interpass limits, to be sure each detail is correct. This is:","reviewing the fine, detailed aspects of work processes",["ignoring the details","skimming quickly","guessing"],"Attention to detail.")
H("823.d.1.F",4,"A small error in a welding procedure, such as the wrong electrode, can:","cause a failed weld and costly rework",["improve quality","have no effect","save money"],"Details matter.")
H("823.d.1.G",3,"After several pipe welds fail inspection, a lead compares the failed welds, notices they were all made after the machine was moved and traces the problem to a poor ground. She is:","evaluating operations and identifying causes and patterns",["blaming people","ignoring data","guessing"],"Systematic analysis.")
H("823.d.1.G",4,"Which approach best identifies the cause of repeated weld defects?","look for patterns across the failed welds",["ignore the failures","blame the newest welder","skip the inspection"],"Patterns reveal causes.")
H("823.d.1.H",3,"A welder follows the shop's written procedure, then adds the supervisor's verbal change to the form. She is:","following written and oral instructions and business practices",["ignoring instructions","skipping documentation","working alone"],"Adhere to practice.")
H("823.d.1.H",4,"If an oral instruction conflicts with the written procedure, the welder should:","ask the supervisor to clarify and document the change",["follow whichever is easier","ignore both","guess"],"Clarify conflicts.")
H("823.d.1.I",3,"A welder lists tomorrow's jobs, puts the rush order first and plans cutting before welding so the shop stays on schedule. She is:","prioritizing tasks and following schedules",["procrastinating","ignoring tasks","working randomly"],"Prioritization.")
H("823.d.1.I",4,"When two jobs are due at the same time, a welder should:","ask which one is more urgent and plan accordingly",["start both and finish neither","skip both","choose without asking"],"Prioritize with input.")
H("823.d.2.A",3,"Before pressing the trigger, Joel inspects the machine, checks the ground and clears flammables. He is:","using welding equipment according to safety standards",["ignoring standards","selling equipment","moving equipment"],"Equipment safety.")
H("823.d.2.A",4,"If a welder smells burning insulation near the machine, the best response is to:","shut it down and report it",["keep welding","ignore it","splash water on it"],"Electrical hazard.")
H("823.d.2.B",3,"Oily rags, spent solvents and used flux are collected in labeled bins for pickup. This shows how to:","identify and properly dispose of hazardous materials",["ignore waste","burn waste","dump waste"],"Proper disposal.")
H("823.d.2.B",4,"The safety data sheet for a cleaning solvent tells a welder:","its hazards, handling and disposal needs",["its price","its color only","nothing useful"],"SDS gives hazards.")
H("823.d.2.C",3,"A shop's recycling program for scrap metal supports:","conservation of resources and less landfill",["more landfill","waste of energy","higher pollution"],"Recycling conserves.")
H("823.d.2.C",4,"Which welding by-product is commonly recycled?","scrap metal off-cuts",["welding smoke","arc light","slag dust only"],"Metal scrap is recycled.")
H("823.d.2.D",3,"A welder chooses a respirator for fumes, gloves rated for heat and a helmet with the correct lens. These are:","appropriate personal protective equipment",["unneeded extras","fashion items","office supplies"],"PPE selection.")
H("823.d.2.D",4,"When grinding after welding, the welder should add:","a face shield over safety glasses",["no protection","sandals","a hat only"],"Grinding adds flying debris.")
H("823.d.3.A",3,"Given a drawing and the stock, Ravi cuts, fits and welds a utility trailer with only an occasional question to the instructor. He is:","working independently to fabricate welded projects with minimal assistance",["only following a lead","avoiding responsibility","waiting for help"],"Independence.")
H("823.d.3.A",4,"A welder working independently should still:","inspect the work against the drawing before finishing",["skip inspection","ignore the drawing","guess sizes"],"Self-check.")
H("823.d.3.B",3,"On a class project, three students divide tasks, share tools and review each other's welds before assembly. They are:","working collaboratively to complete a project",["competing","working alone","avoiding tasks"],"Collaboration.")
H("823.d.3.B",4,"The best way for a team to finish a project on time is to:","assign roles and communicate progress",["work at random","avoid talking","ignore deadlines"],"Roles and communication.")
H("823.d.3.C",3,"When a wire welder will not feed, Elena checks the drive rolls, the liner and the spool brake in order. She is:","troubleshooting equipment",["selling equipment","painting equipment","ignoring equipment"],"Troubleshooting is methodical.")
H("823.d.3.C",4,"A weld with heavy porosity may be traced to:","a shielding gas problem or contaminated metal",["too much paint on the helmet","the shop's lights","the welder's shoes"],"Common causes.")
H("823.d.4.A",3,"An inspector uses a flashlight, a mirror, a gauge and a camera to examine a weld, then records what she finds. She is explaining:","weld inspection processes",["cooking methods","painting methods","packing methods"],"Inspection process.")
H("823.d.4.A",4,"A destructive test used to check weld quality is:","a guided bend test",["a visual look only","a photo","a paint test"],"Bend tests break samples.")
H("823.d.4.B",3,"A student welds a test coupon to meet the acceptance criteria in a structural welding code. She is producing:","acceptable weldments to industry code standards",["random welds","guessed welds","unfinished welds"],"Code compliance.")
H("823.d.4.B",4,"A weld that meets code has defects within:","the code's acceptance limits",["no limits","any size","the welder's opinion"],"Codes set limits.")
H("823.d.5.A",3,"Before lighting a torch, Brin checks for flammables, wears the correct PPE and has a spark lighter ready. She is:","using safe operating practices",["ignoring risks","skipping steps","guessing"],"Torch safety.")
H("823.d.5.A",4,"A torch that backfires with a pop should be:","shut off and inspected before relighting",["relit immediately","left on","ignored"],"Backfires indicate a problem.")
H("823.d.5.B",3,"At the end of the day, the oxygen and fuel gas cylinders are valved off, capped and chained upright. This is:","safe handling of compressed gases",["unsafe handling","careless handling","random handling"],"Cylinder handling.")
H("823.d.5.B",4,"Moving a cylinder with its cap off by rolling it on the valve is:","unsafe because the valve can break",["safe","acceptable","recommended"],"Cap on, secure.")
H("823.d.5.C",3,"A student connects the regulators, hoses, check valves and torch and tests for leaks with soapy water. This is:","assembling the components for oxy-fuel cutting",["dismantling","cleaning","packing"],"Assemble then test.")
H("823.d.5.C",4,"A common way to check a connection for gas leaks is with:","a soapy water solution",["an open flame","a paper towel","paint"],"Bubbles reveal leaks.")
H("823.d.5.D",3,"Before piercing, cutting a straight line or cutting a bevel, a student sets the tip, pressures and torch angle for the job. This is:","proper set-up for cutting techniques",["a cleanup","a shutdown","a delay"],"Set-up per technique.")
H("823.d.5.D",4,"To cut a bevel, the torch is tilted to:","the angle required for the joint preparation",["a random angle","vertical only","upside down"],"Match the angle.")
H("823.d.5.E",3,"Looking at two cut edges, one smooth and square and the other gouged with heavy drag lines, a student decides which is acceptable. She is:","evaluating acceptable and unacceptable cuts",["painting edges","drilling holes","bending metal"],"Evaluate cut quality.")
H("823.d.5.E",4,"Deep gouges and rounded top edges on a cut usually show:","incorrect speed or tip condition",["a perfect cut","cold weather","too much light"],"Cut defects have causes.")
H("823.d.6.A",3,"Before plasma cutting, Omari checks the work clamp, wears a shaded face shield and removes combustibles. He is:","using safe operating practices",["ignoring risks","skipping steps","guessing"],"Plasma safety.")
H("823.d.6.A",4,"A plasma cutter's torch should never be pointed at:","any person",["the work","the table","the floor away from people"],"Torch discipline.")
H("823.d.6.B",3,"A cylinder stored upright, chained and capped is safe. A cylinder lying on the floor without a cap is unsafe. This shows the difference in:","safe and unsafe storage and handling of compressed gases",["paint choices","tool choices","price choices"],"Storage matters.")
H("823.d.6.B",4,"Why must a compressed gas cylinder be secured upright?","a falling cylinder can break the valve and become a projectile",["it looks neater","it keeps gas colder","it saves space only"],"Valve damage is dangerous.")
H("823.d.6.C",3,"A student checks the air pressure, installs the correct consumables and sets the amperage for the plate thickness. This is:","proper set-up for plasma arc cutting",["a cleanup","a shutdown","a repair"],"Set-up before cutting.")
H("823.d.6.C",4,"Installing the wrong nozzle on a plasma torch can cause:","poor cut quality and faster wear",["perfect cuts","no change","better control"],"Match consumables.")
H("823.d.6.D",3,"A student cuts a straight line along a guide, pierces a hole and bevels an edge with a plasma torch. She is demonstrating:","proper plasma cutting techniques",["only welding","only grinding","only painting"],"Plasma techniques.")
H("823.d.6.D",4,"When piercing with a plasma torch, the operator tilts the torch slightly to:","blow molten metal away from the torch and operator",["increase sparks at the operator","cool the plate","stop the arc"],"Tilting protects the torch.")

H("823.d.7.A",3,"Before striking an arc on a pipe weld, Wes dries his gloves, stands on a dry mat and checks his cable ends. He is:","using safe operating practices",["ignoring risks","skipping steps","guessing"],"Stick welding safety.")
H("823.d.7.A",4,"Wet gloves are dangerous for stick welding because they can:","conduct electricity and cause a shock",["improve the grip","insulate the arc","cool the rod"],"Moisture raises shock risk.")
H("823.d.7.B",3,"A welder explains that the arc melts the base metal and the electrode, while the flux coating makes slag and a shielding gas over the pool. She is demonstrating:","shielded metal arc welding principles",["gas welding","brazing","soldering"],"SMAW basics.")
H("823.d.7.B",4,"The slag layer on a stick weld protects the bead by:","slowing cooling and keeping air away",["adding heat","adding color only","burning the metal"],"Slag protects.")
H("823.d.7.C",3,"Maya connects the ground, sets the amperage for a 3/32 in. rod, and dries the rods in a rod oven. This is:","proper set-up for shielded metal arc welding",["a shutdown","a repair","a purchase"],"Set-up details.")
H("823.d.7.C",4,"Setting the current too low for the electrode can cause:","poor penetration and a sticking rod",["too much penetration","no heat","a faster weld"],"Low amperage causes sticking.")
H("823.d.7.D",3,"For a root pass on pipe, a welder picks an E6010 and for the fill passes an E7018. She is:","selecting appropriate electrodes for the base metal",["choosing at random","choosing the cheapest","choosing by color"],"Electrode selection.")
H("823.d.7.D",4,"Low-hydrogen electrodes like E7018 are used when:","strength and crack resistance are required",["no strength is needed","speed alone matters","the metal is wet"],"Low hydrogen reduces cracking.")
H("823.d.7.E",3,"A welder runs a fillet on a T-joint and a groove weld on a beveled butt joint, matching the weld size to the print. She is performing:","fillet and groove welds to industry-accepted standards",["tack welds only","cutting only","painting only"],"Standard welds.")
H("823.d.7.E",4,"A fillet weld's size is measured as the:","length of its leg",["color of its slag","weight of its rod","time it takes"],"Leg size.")
H("823.d.7.F",3,"A thick plate needs several layers stacked in order, cleaning between each. This is:","a multiple pass weld",["a tack weld","a spot weld","a flange weld"],"Multiple passes.")
H("823.d.7.F",4,"The first pass in a multiple pass groove weld is the:","root pass",["cap pass","filler pass","sealing pass only"],"Root first.")
H("823.d.7.G",3,"Before welding, a student bevels the plate edges, grinds off mill scale and sets the root opening. She is:","preparing joints for welding",["painting joints","cutting rods","storing rods"],"Joint prep.")
H("823.d.7.G",4,"A root opening in a groove joint allows:","penetration to the bottom of the joint",["less penetration","no filler","a shorter arc"],"Root opening aids fusion.")
H("823.d.7.H",3,"A welder warms thick carbon steel before welding and lets it cool slowly afterward. This explains:","preheating and postheating",["painting","cleaning","packing"],"Heat treatment around welding.")
H("823.d.7.H",4,"A main reason for preheating is to:","slow cooling and reduce cracking",["speed cooling","add color","reduce current"],"Preheat prevents cracks.")
H("823.d.8.A",3,"Before running wire, Luz checks the gas supply, the drive rolls and the work area for flammables. She is:","using safe operating practices",["ignoring risks","skipping steps","guessing"],"GMAW safety.")
H("823.d.8.A",4,"A hot welding gun nozzle should be:","handled with gloves and cooled before changing",["touched bare-handed","dunked in cold water","thrown across the shop"],"Hot parts burn.")
H("823.d.8.B",3,"A student explains that the machine feeds a solid wire at a set speed while an inert or mixed gas shields the molten pool. She is demonstrating:","gas metal arc welding principles",["stick welding","gas cutting","brazing"],"GMAW principles.")
H("823.d.8.B",4,"In GMAW, the voltage setting mainly controls the:","arc length and bead width",["wire color","gas cost","helmet shade"],"Voltage affects the arc.")
H("823.d.8.C",3,"After loading the spool, Noel sets the gas flow, the voltage and the wire speed for 1/4 in. plate. This is:","proper set-up for gas metal arc welding",["tear-down","repair","bidding"],"Set-up before welding.")
H("823.d.8.C",4,"Too little shielding gas flow can cause:","porosity in the weld",["a stronger weld","no heat","a clean bead"],"Gas protects the pool.")
H("823.d.8.D",3,"Welding stainless steel with GMAW, a welder picks a stainless wire and a suitable gas mix. She is:","selecting appropriate filler metals for the base metal",["choosing randomly","choosing the cheapest","choosing by weight"],"Match filler to base.")
H("823.d.8.D",4,"A good filler wire for welding mild steel is:","ER70S-6",["ER4043","ER308L only","brass"],"Common mild steel wire.")
H("823.d.8.E",3,"A student welds fillet and groove joints in flat, horizontal, vertical and overhead positions to meet a code standard. She is performing:","welds in all positions to industry standards",["only flat welds","only tacks","only cuts"],"All positions.")
H("823.d.8.E",4,"Vertical-up welding with GMAW typically uses:","lower heat settings and a controlled weave",["maximum heat","no gas","a backhand only technique with no weave"],"Control the puddle.")
H("823.d.9.A",3,"Before running flux cored wire inside, Wren turns on fume extraction and checks the work area for flammables. She is:","using safe operating practices",["ignoring risks","skipping steps","guessing"],"FCAW safety.")
H("823.d.9.A",4,"Flux cored welding makes more smoke, so the best control is:","ventilation or local fume extraction",["no airflow","a closed door","extra heat"],"Fumes need removal.")
H("823.d.9.B",3,"A student explains why self-shielded wire works outdoors and then compares bead appearance with a gas-shielded wire. She is employing and appraising:","flux cored arc welding principles",["gas cutting","brazing","soldering"],"Appraisal of FCAW.")
H("823.d.9.B",4,"Gas-shielded flux cored wire generally produces:","less spatter and a smoother bead than self-shielded wire",["more spatter","no slag","no fumes"],"Gas-shielded is cleaner.")
H("823.d.9.C",3,"After installing a knurled drive roll, the welder sets the voltage, wire speed and polarity for the wire. This is:","proper set-up for flux cored arc welding",["a shutdown","a repair","a bid"],"Knurled rolls grip tubular wire.")
H("823.d.9.C",4,"Flux cored wire is fed with knurled or V-knurl drive rolls because the tubular wire:","would crush under smooth rolls",["is too hard","needs more heat","is a solid rod"],"Tubular wire crushes easily.")
H("823.d.9.D",3,"A welder appraises two wires for a structural job and decides on E71T-1 for out-of-position welds. She is:","appraising appropriate filler metal for the base metal",["choosing randomly","choosing by price only","choosing by color"],"Filler appraisal.")
H("823.d.9.D",4,"For wind outdoors on mild steel, a welder most likely prefers:","self-shielded flux cored wire",["gas shielded solid wire only","tungsten","brazing rod"],"No gas to blow away.")
H("823.d.9.E",3,"A student makes a T-joint fillet and a beveled groove weld with flux cored wire on 3/8 in. plate. She is performing:","fillet and groove welds",["only tack welds","only cutting","only painting"],"Basic welds.")
H("823.d.9.E",4,"The slag over a flux cored weld is removed with:","a chipping hammer and wire brush",["a paint brush","a sponge","a magnet"],"Slag removal.")
H("823.d.9.F",3,"For a code test, a welder passes flux cored welds in each assigned position. This is:","welding in all appropriate positions per industry standards",["only the easiest position","only flat","only overhead"],"Position coverage.")
H("823.d.9.F",4,"A welder qualified in a more difficult position, such as vertical, is often also:","qualified for easier positions covered by the code",["disqualified for flat","unable to weld flat","limited to one weld"],"Higher positions can cover lower ones.")
H("823.d.10.A",3,"Before TIG welding aluminum, Pia checks the gas hose, wears the right lens and moves chlorinated cleaners away. She is:","using safe operating practices",["ignoring risks","skipping steps","guessing"],"GTAW safety.")
H("823.d.10.A",4,"A TIG welder avoids grinding thoriated tungsten without dust control because:","the dust is a hazard if inhaled",["it is a coolant","it is harmless","it is decorative"],"Control grinding dust.")
H("823.d.10.B",3,"A welder explains that a non-consumable tungsten electrode makes the arc while a separate filler rod is added by hand and argon shields the pool. She is demonstrating:","gas tungsten arc welding principles",["stick welding","oxy-fuel cutting","plasma cutting"],"GTAW basics.")
H("823.d.10.B",4,"The tungsten electrode in TIG welding is called non-consumable because it:","does not melt into the weld",["is eaten by the arc","is wire","is slag"],"Tungsten stays in the torch.")
H("823.d.10.C",3,"After grinding the tungsten to a taper and selecting the cup size, the welder sets the current, gas flow and pedal. This is:","proper set-up for gas tungsten arc welding",["a shutdown","a repair","a bid"],"Set-up details.")
H("823.d.10.C",4,"The tungsten should be ground with the marks running:","lengthwise along the electrode",["around the electrode","at random","across the tip"],"Lengthwise grinding steadies the arc.")
H("823.d.10.D",3,"For welding 304 stainless, a welder chooses ER308L filler rod. She is:","selecting appropriate filler metal for the base metal",["choosing randomly","choosing by price","choosing by weight"],"Filler matches base.")
H("823.d.10.D",4,"A filler commonly used on 6061 aluminum with TIG is:","ER4043 or ER5356",["ER70S-6","brass rod","copper wire"],"Aluminum fillers.")
H("823.d.10.E",3,"A student welds a TIG fillet and groove in the flat, horizontal, vertical and overhead positions to meet a standard. She is:","welding in all appropriate positions per industry standards",["only flat","only tacking","only cutting"],"All-position TIG.")
H("823.d.10.E",4,"In vertical-up TIG welding, the welder keeps the puddle small to:","prevent it from sagging",["increase sagging","add spatter","stop the arc"],"Small puddles resist gravity.")
H("823.d.11.A",3,"A student points out a combination square, a scribe, a center punch, dividers and a soapstone on the layout bench. She is:","identifying layout tools",["identifying welding rods","identifying gases","identifying PPE"],"Layout tools.")
H("823.d.11.A",4,"A scribe is used in layout to:","mark a fine line on metal",["cool metal","clean slag","melt metal"],"Scribes mark lines.")
H("823.d.11.B",3,"From a blueprint, Teo lays out hole centers and cut lines on a plate with a scale, scribe and center punch. He is:","performing a part layout on plate",["welding the plate","painting the plate","packing the plate"],"Plate layout.")
H("823.d.11.B",4,"Before cutting a plate, the layout lines are checked against the print for:","accuracy of dimensions and locations",["color","price","weight only"],"Check before cutting.")
H("823.d.11.C",3,"Using a wrap-around and a blueprint, a student marks the cut line for a pipe fitting on a section of pipe. She is:","performing a layout of a pipe fitting",["welding a fitting","cleaning a fitting","buying a fitting"],"Pipe layout.")
H("823.d.11.C",4,"To mark a cutline around a pipe, a fitter often uses:","a wrap-around template",["a tape and guess","a paintbrush","a hammer only"],"Wrap-arounds mark straight lines.")
H("823.d.11.D",3,"Following the blueprint, a student cuts, fits, tacks and welds the parts of a frame in the right order. She is performing:","an assembly according to a blueprint",["a random build","a guess","a copy of a coworker"],"Assemble to print.")
H("823.d.11.D",4,"Before final welding an assembly, the fitter should:","check the fit and squareness against the blueprint",["skip checks","weld first","ignore dimensions"],"Verify first.")

B.balance()
B.save(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "..", "batches", "cte_119.jsonl"))
